# Fixed 2026-10-07, defect 458, lane b14-check: the shape beside it written
# with a dot. Symptom: `c.end_lease()` on a lease cell was told *this
# argument is not such a cell*. `end_lease` changes its first argument, and
# the dotted form hides the `@` it owes, which is what any such call is told.

function main()
    x = "abc"
    c: cstr = x.lease()
    c.end_lease()  #~ ufcs_on_mutable
